{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I had oxen and asses and sheep.</b> He mentioned his wealth by way of the many through the few, so as not to boast, in the manner of what is written (Jeremiah 9:22): ״אל יתהלל עשיר בעשרו״ — let not the rich man boast in his wealth. And so is the way of the righteous, that they diminish themselves and all that is theirs; but the wicked exalt themselves and all that is theirs, such as Esav, who said: ״יש לי רב״ — I have plenty." "<b>And it was.</b> It would have been proper for Scripture to put the sheep first, for so is the way of Scriptural passages to put them first, because it is the most honored and choice species among all animals — as it is written of Abraham (Genesis 12:16): ״ולאברם היטיב בעבורה ויהי לו צאן ובקר״. Also of Isaac it is written (Genesis 26:14): ״ויהי לו מקנה צאן ומקנה בקר ועבודה רבה״. Also of Jacob it is written (Genesis 30:43): ״ויהי לו צאן רבות ושפחות ועבדים וגמלים וחמורים״ — the species of sheep preceding all the other animals. And the reason he did not put it first in this verse is that he did not wish to open with sheep for him, because through sheep Esav was emptied of the blessings and Jacob merited them, in the manner of what is written: ״לך נא אל הצאן״. But when the messengers returned to Jacob, he put the sheep first: ״ויחץ את העם אשר אתו ואת הצאן ואת הבקר וגו׳״. Also after he was appeased toward him and accepted his gift, he put it first — and that is what he said: ״אדני יודע כי הילדים רכים והצאן והבקר עלות עלי״." "<b>And by way of the Midrash.</b> ״ויהי לי שור וחמור״ — why did he put the ox first? It was a hint to him that Joseph had already been born, he who is the adversary of Esav; as it is written (Obadiah 1:18): ״והיה בית יעקב אש ובית יוסף להבה ובית עשו לקש ודלקו בהם ואכלום״. Joseph is called an ox, as it is stated (Deuteronomy 33:17): ״בכור שורו הדר לו״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:17:07.366696208Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}